# component: sidebar
# decisions: A11Y-2, A11Y-17, A11Y-18, API-29, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6, FRM-4, INT-11, LAY-13, LAY-16, OVL-16, VOI-1
# hunks:
#   API-29: `SidebarMenuButton` styles its own open state — `aria-expanded:` and
#     `data-popup-open:` take the `sidebar-accent` fill and ink — so a menu trigger such as the
#     user menu needs no className (MK, 2026-09-25).
#   BRD-1: the floating variant's inner surface swaps upstream's
#     `group-data-[variant=floating]:ring-1 …:ring-sidebar-border` box-shadow outline for a real
#     `…:border …:border-sidebar-border` — the sidebar's own hairline ink, so the edge matches the
#     `sidebar` variant's `border-e`. The floating sidebar is a floating surface, and MK extended
#     BRD-1 to it on 23-09-2026. The container already budgets `+2px` for the collapsed width.
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `outline-hidden` and `focus-visible:ring-2` are removed from all five controls
#     that carry them — `SidebarGroupLabel`, `SidebarGroupAction`, `SidebarMenuButton`,
#     `SidebarMenuAction` and `SidebarMenuSubButton`. `outline-hidden` is the v3 spelling of 'no
#     outline': upstream suppresses the browser's and paints its own 2px ring instead, and this
#     system does the opposite. `ring-sidebar-ring` is left in place on each — it is a colour
#     with no ring width behind it any more, it paints nothing, and removing it would take the
#     `--sidebar-ring` token's only reference with it.
#   FRM-4: `disabled:pointer-events-none` and `aria-disabled:pointer-events-none` are dropped
#     from `SidebarMenuButton` and `SidebarMenuSubButton`, so a disabled nav row stays hoverable
#     and a Tooltip can explain why. Both opacity halves stay.
#   A11Y-2: `md:after:hidden` is dropped from `SidebarMenuAction` and `SidebarGroupAction`.
#     Both are `w-5` (20px) squares, which is under the 24px floor, and upstream already solves
#     that the way A11Y-2 asks — with an invisible `after:absolute after:-inset-2` hit area — and
#     then switches the area OFF again at `md` and above. Measured with a real
#     `document.elementFromPoint` probe over compiled Tailwind: 36x36 with 0/5 obstruction misses
#     at 390px, and 20x20 at 1280px, i.e. 4px under the floor at EVERY desktop width. Nothing in
#     this repository could have seen it — the global geometry lane sweeps at 320px only, where
#     `md:` never applies. § 5.2 lists `sidebar` under A11Y-2 as a CANDIDATE to audit rather than
#     an assignment; this is that audit finding a real violation, so the exception is applied. The
#     hit area is the only thing that changes: the visible 20px box, its position and its hover
#     wash are upstream's. `sidebar.test.tsx` measures both controls at both widths.
#   A11Y-17: `SidebarMenuButton` takes `badge` and `badgeLabel`. The count joins the control's
#     name through a comma-free `sr-only` suffix (" 12 unread"), so the name reads
#     "Inbox 12 unread"; an A11Y-5 `sr-only ", "` separator was measured to read "Inbox , 12
#     unread" once CSS blockifies the flex children (accname step 2F), and the row was amended
#     to the suffix. `badgeLabel` defaults to a string or number `badge`. The button renders the
#     visual `SidebarMenuBadge` as its upstream sibling, so every `peer-*/menu-button` recipe on
#     the badge still applies, and `SidebarMenuBadge` is now `aria-hidden` wherever it is used.
#     While a count is present the label (`span:nth-last-child(2)`) keeps upstream's `truncate`,
#     because the suffix is now the last span. The collapsed tooltip carries the same count.
#     Badge padding: `group-has-data-[sidebar=menu-badge]/menu-item:pe-8`, beside upstream's
#     menu-action `pe-8`, and `pe-12` when the badge is `data-badge-size="lg"` (a string or
#     number badge of three or more characters), so a long label stops short of the count.
#   A11Y-18: `SidebarMenuButton` sets `aria-current="page"` when `isActive` and `render` is a
#     link (an `<a>`, or any element carrying `href`). A button never gets it, and a caller's own
#     `aria-current` wins.
#   INT-11: the Mod+B handler returns early when the event is already `defaultPrevented` or
#     started in an editable target — `isEditableTarget` from `@/components/ui/use-platform`
#     (input, textarea, select, contenteditable; the same guard `shortcut-overlay` uses). The
#     provider takes `keyboardShortcut` (default upstream's "b"; `false` attaches no listener).
#   LAY-13: static-shell state. New exports `SidebarStateScript` — an inline `<head>` script that
#     reads the cookie, sets `data-sidebar-state="collapsed"` on `<html>`, and gives the desktop
#     panel (`[data-slot=sidebar][data-state]`) the collapsed `data-state` and the caller's
#     `data-collapsible` as the parser inserts it (a MutationObserver that disconnects on the first
#     hit or at DOMContentLoaded), so upstream's own `group-data-*`/`peer-data-*` recipes paint it
#     collapsed; the cookie name is written through a `<`-escaped JSON literal — and
#     `useSidebarCookieOpen(cookieName?)`, the `[open, setOpen]` pair for a controlled provider.
#     The uncontrolled provider's initial state reads the `<html>` mark (falling back to
#     `defaultOpen`), so the client's hydration render equals the pre-painted DOM, and every
#     toggle keeps an existing mark in step. The cookie write moves into `writeSidebarCookie`,
#     gains `SameSite=Lax`, and happens only when the provider is uncontrolled.
#   LAY-16: `SidebarMenuSkeleton`'s `Math.random()` width in a state initialiser becomes a fixed
#     cycle (70%, 55%, 85%, 60%, 75%) picked by a new `index` prop, so server and client markup
#     agree and the docs preview no longer has to mount it after hydration.
#   OVL-16: the mobile panel's `SheetContent` adds `data-[side=left]:w-(--sidebar-width)` and
#     `data-[side=right]:w-(--sidebar-width)`. The Sheet's side widths are keyed on `data-side`,
#     which outranks the plain `w-(--sidebar-width)` upstream relies on; restating the width on the
#     same variant keeps the sheet at SIDEBAR_WIDTH_MOBILE (18rem) whatever width OVL-16's sheet
#     sizes give a side sheet, so the scrim beside it stays tappable.
#   VOI-1: "Toggle Sidebar" becomes "Toggle sidebar" in `SidebarTrigger`'s `sr-only` label and on
#     `SidebarRail`'s `aria-label` and `title`, and both take `triggerLabel` to override it.
#   registry layout (DOC-1): `@/hooks/use-mobile` becomes `@/components/ui/use-mobile`. Hooks are
#     `registry:hook` items alongside the components in this registry, which is the path the
#     three-copy model and `shadcn add @vegastack/use-mobile` both use.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
